  "title": "The Last Note on the Bench",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "silent emotional stories",
  "premise": "A busker wants to finish a melody, but the single listener leaves before the final note. The busker plays it anyway; a folded paper bird left on the bench opens to show the listener’s drawing of the performance, and the busker places it beside the case.",
  "hook": "The final note still belongs here.",
  "visible_action": "Listener rises and exits; musician hesitates then plays; paper bird unfolds; drawing catches a small pool of light.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A moment can matter even when its ending is quiet.",
  "gate": "Use an original melody and original drawing; do not infer a stranger’s feelings beyond the visible fictional gesture.",
  "evidence_class": "fictional_demonstration",
